    "result_text": "All 56 tests pass. The change is complete and green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `salutation` feature on the `POST /api/owners` + `GET /api/owners/{id}` flow, following the existing derived-field conventions in this Spring Boot app.\n\n**What I changed:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `title` input property to the `OwnerFields` schema and a read-only derived `salutation` property to the `Owner` schema. (DTOs are generated from this spec at build time.)\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a persisted `title` column (field + getter/setter) and a `@Transient getSalutation()` method returning `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when the title is absent/blank (mirrors how `telephoneDisplay`, `checkDigit`, and `identityKey` auto-map from transient getters).\n\n3. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,postgres,mysql}/schema.sql`** \u2014 Added the `title` column to the `owners` table (tests run on hsqldb; the rest kept consistent).\n\nNo mapper changes were needed \u2014 MapStruct auto-maps `title` (request \u2192 entity \u2192 response) and `salutation` (from `getSalutation()`) by name.\n\n**Verification:** `Cp45Tests` (salutation) passes, and the full suite is green \u2014 `Tests run: 56, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
